# General Principles

## Philosophy
- Think first, build second
- Explicit over implicit
- Small, focused commits
- Code is documentation

## Code Style
- Minimize comments - name things clearly instead
- No separate .md files - docs live in cursor rules only
- Delete dead code immediately
- One concept per file

## Code Minimalism
- Less code is always better
- Delete unused components immediately
- No dead code, no commented-out code
- If a component isn't used, it doesn't exist
- Every line must earn its place

## Process
```
1. Understand the requirement fully
2. Check existing patterns in codebase
3. Implement minimal solution
4. Refactor only if needed
```

## Anti-patterns
```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Comment explaining obvious code
// Increment counter by 1
counter++;

// ✅ Good: Self-documenting name
const nextPageIndex = currentPageIndex + 1;

// ❌ Bad: Magic values
if (status === 3) { ... }

// ✅ Good: Named constants
if (status === BookingStatus.CONFIRMED) { ... }
```

## Commits
```
feat(resource): add tutor availability endpoint
fix(booking): handle timezone edge case
refactor(auth): extract token validation
```
